            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "One where the deck itself hinges at the middle in addition to the handle folding down, roughly halving the storage footprint again. The mechanism originated in the KingSmith range and is now widely copied. It stores far smaller and costs you some usable deck length, adds thickness and price, and puts a hinge directly under your stride.",
          },
